# Remote terminal safety

The terminal is a narrow bridge to the pier. Treat every command as running on the remote host,
even when the input arrives from a Bluetooth keyboard or trackball on the tablet.

- Keep the long-lived agent inside `tmux`; Mosh provides transport roaming, not process survival.
- Prefer the repository launcher, `./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh cursor-agent ...`, so the project's
  enclosure and durable auth mapping stay in one place.
- Inspect a target before changing it. Do not use destructive commands, force Git operations,
  firewall changes, or `nixos-rebuild` without an explicit human approval at the pier.
- Do not print, commit, or paste auth files, API keys, cookies, private keys, or the contents of
  ignored `loops/` state.
- A model setting in a local CLI cache is not project policy. Record configuration separately from
  verified runtime identity in session logs, following `.claude/rules/session-log-provenance.md`.

When the network drops, reconnect Mosh and attach to the existing tmux session before deciding
whether work was lost.
